= Galleon Fleet

The Commonwealth Army Ministry is lobbying for a naval modernization program centered on the construction of a new fleet of war-galleons, the Galleon Fleet. The propertied parties are united in support, and the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is likely to yield to right-wing pressure. A vote on the project is expected once a new government is formed after the May elections.

This presents us with an opportunity: we could campaign against the ship’s construction and demand its cancellation in favor of greater social spending. The workers have rallied behind our slogan, "Children's Meals Instead of War-Galleons", but the mire of coalition politics may yet force us to backtrack—should we enter government.

- @anti_ship: Children's meals instead of war-galleons!
- @pro_ship: Stay relatively silent on the matter—we can’t break a promise we never made.

@anti_ship
on-arrival: commons_marcher += 4*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 2*(1-dissent); panzerkreuzer_campaign = 1

Our catchy slogan has helped rally the workers’ vote and limit defections to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

@pro_ship
on-arrival: commons_collectivist += 2; disfavored_collectivist += 2; labor_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 5; collectivist_relation -= 6; panzerkreuzer_campaign = 0

Our silence has left the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> as the sole party vocally opposing the ship’s construction—and they waste no time accusing us of betrayal. The Left and Labor factions voice their displeasure.